<svelte:head><title>Help — WantMyTime</title></svelte:head><section class="article-page"><p class="eyebrow">Help</p><h1 class="page-heading">A few useful answers.</h1><div class="faq"><details><summary>Should my friends use my link?</summary><p>No need. Friends already have your number and get your time free. Your link is for people you don’t know yet: the ones who find you online and ask for a call.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need to be a professional?</summary><p>No. You do need to follow the rules that apply to what you provide.</p></details><details><summary>Do I have to say what I can help with?</summary><p>No. People opening your link already chose you.</p></details><details><summary>Can I choose the price?</summary><p>Yes. You can set a price or let people make one offer.</p></details><details><summary>Does the visitor need an account?</summary><p>A full seller account is not required. Secure email access is needed for cross-device management.</p></details><details><summary>When does money reach my bank?</summary><p>About 3 hours after each session ends. WantMyTime holds the buyer’s payment until the session is over and the buyer’s 2 hours to report a problem have passed, then sends your share to the bank account you added under Settings › Payouts. If a problem is reported, that payout waits until WantMyTime has looked at it. Most banks show the money within minutes.</p></details><details><summary>Where does the conversation happen?</summary><p>In a private meeting link supplied for that booking.</p></details><details><summary>Can I pause my link?</summary><p>Yes. Existing bookings should stay accessible.</p></details><details><summary>What if a payment or booking goes wrong?</summary><p>Report it from your booking page. Buyers have until 2 hours after the end of the session; the seller isn’t paid until the problem is reviewed, and WantMyTime can refund part or all of the payment.</p></details></div></section>
